<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who a TidalFit swim spa is for</h2>
        <p>A TidalFit exercise pool is for families who want swimming, exercise and hydrotherapy at home but don't have the yard, budget or swim season for a full pool. In Utah that last point matters: a heated, covered swim spa works in January, not just July. The True Variable Speed swim current adjusts from gentle to challenging, so beginners, kids and serious swimmers can all use it.</p>
        <h2>Pick your size</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Active EP-12</strong> and <strong>ActivePlus EP-12</strong> are about 12 feet long and 7.6 feet wide with 4 seats. The Active EP-12 is 45 inches deep, holds about 1,195 gallons and has 16 jets, while the ActivePlus steps up to 28 Helix jets, with a BellagioFall water feature available. The <strong>Pro EP-15</strong> is about 15 feet long and 60 inches deep, holds about 2,075 gallons, and is the one to choose if laps are your priority. TidalFit also makes standalone hot tubs (DTL-6, DTL-8, DT-19 and DT-21).</p>
        <h2>Electrical, pad and installation</h2>
        <p>TidalFit exercise pools use a 5.5 kW heater on a dedicated 240V circuit. They're heavy. Using the manufacturer's capacities and dry weights, an Active EP-12 weighs roughly 11,700 pounds filled and a Pro EP-15 roughly 19,700 pounds, before anyone gets in, so a properly engineered concrete pad is essential. Plan for steps too: TidalFit offers a <a href="/steps/">5-step unit</a>. Our <a href="/guides/swim-spa-vs-pool-utah/">Swim Spa vs Pool in Utah</a> guide covers costs, space and maintenance.</p>
        <h2>See TidalFit in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit. Ask us about <a href="/financing/">financing</a> if you'd like to spread out the cost.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

